            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0168" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg52"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/827.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Chargé d’Affaires
                        at Tokyo</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-10-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 27, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your October 22. You may convey on an appropriate occasion to the Foreign Office
                    the Department’s appreciation of the information therein, and an assurance of
                    the entire confidence of this Government in Japan’s policy in China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
